{{! kimi-agent.md.tmpl: the per-run Kimi Code agent file, <run>/inputs/agent.md, passed with --agent-file.
  It carries the brief and a tools allowlist. kimi -p runs under the auto permission policy
  (bypass_equivalent: true in runtimes/kimi-code.yaml), so the allowlist and static deny rules from a
  user-owned KIMI_CODE_HOME are the only prevention; Kimi stays rung D until conformance verifies them.
  Frontmatter fields (name, description, tools, disallowedTools, subagents): verification_status
  documented. Kimi renders dollar-brace variables in the body and leaves unknown ones verbatim, so the
  brief bytes survive (verify by probe).
  tools and disallowed_tools come from the seat contract's execution class; subagents stays empty.
  brief_markdown is the rendered brief from templates/prompts/brief.md.tmpl, byte for byte. }}
---
name: keel-{{seat}}
description: keel {{seat}} seat for run {{run_id}}. Selected with --agent-file; not for delegation.
tools:
{{#tools}}
  - {{.}}
{{/tools}}
disallowedTools:
{{#disallowed_tools}}
  - {{.}}
{{/disallowed_tools}}
subagents: []
---

You hold the keel {{seat}} seat for run {{run_id}}. Follow the `keel-{{skill}}` skill. The brief below is
your whole contract. ACK before your first edit on the submit channel it names.

{{brief_markdown}}
